  <field_wiki_entry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Large terrestrial squirrel native to the lowland forests of Borneo, known for its extremely bushy tail and powerful jaws. Despite its common name, it is primarily a forest-floor rodent that forages among dense vegetation and fallen material for hard seeds, nuts, and other food items.</field_wiki_entry>
